# Bodied factories read a parameter once — the authoring route, accepted by Dev on 2026-09-18 ("Accept,
# the authoring route for the three bodied factories first"), on b404d7e (623 / 44 green).
#
# ONE CONCEPT: step 3's guarantee (a factory argument is evaluated at most once) rests on the factory
# BODY being the prelude. Three bodied factories read a parameter at two sites, so the argument could be
# evaluated twice. The fix is in drake, not the engine, by the mechanism the guarantee already rests on:
#   Domain          the second site reads the MEMBER the first site bound — `TypeDictionary(typeDefinition)`
#   TypeDictionary  `loc domainDefinition TypeDefinition _domainDefinition`, both sites read the loc
#   DomainLineOf    `loc definition TypeDefinition _definition`, both sites read the loc
# `loc x T _x` is step 2's method prelude, AUTHORED — the idiom for a bodied factory that reads a parameter
# more than once. A lazy binding is read once and remembered; the parameter is forced on its first read.
#
# Why not the engine: the method prelude works because a method body reads the bare name; a factory body
# reads the underscore name (the bare name is the member), so an engine prelude would need a third name
# and a parameter rename, and `_namePackage = …` at every call site forbids the rename. Three drake lines
# make the promise true; the language does not hide a parameter read twice.
#
# TRIO by the compiled CLIs (classes from Dev's run 2 = b404d7e engine and parser, overlay of main + test
# resources): DrakeCLI parse -> JSON (Domain 1 line; TypeDictionary and DomainLineOf gain one Local),
# GeneratorCLI generate -> Scala (the three diffs are exactly the renames plus one `lazy val` each; the
# CLI's trailing blank line stripped to the committed style, which the gate normalizes anyway),
# DrakeCLI check over src/main/resources: the three round-trip. No engine change, no test change.
#
# RUN: expected 623 tests / 44 suites, all green; every headline unchanged (surface losses 5: the lambda in
# TypeDictionary was an opaque string before and is one still).
